  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "Let $f_{1}:(0, \\infty) \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}$ and $f_{2}:(0, \\infty) \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}$ be defined by\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\nf_{1}(x)=\\int_{0}^{x} \\prod_{j=1}^{21}(t-j)^{j} d t, \\quad x>0\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\nand\r\n\r\n$\r\n\r\nf_{2}(x)=98(x-1)^{50}-600(x-1)^{49}+2450, \\quad x>0\r\n\r\n$\r\n\r\nwhere, for any positive integer $n$ and real numbers $a_{1}, a_{2}, \\ldots, a_{n}, \\prod_{i=1}^{n} a_{i}$ denotes the product of $a_{1}, a_{2}, \\ldots, a_{n} .$ Let $m_{i}$ and $n_{i}$, respectively, denote the number of points of local minima and the number of points of local maxima of function $f_{i}, i=1,2$, in the interval $(0, \\infty)$.\r\n\r\nThe value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is _____.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "57",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><munderover><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>x</mi></munderover><mfenced><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>......</mn><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>21</mn></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mn>1</mn></msub><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>.....</mn><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>21</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>21</mn></msup></math></p><p>Checking critical points</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/96d8ba46-cf0d-4b82-ad3b-c1cd70463a9a-image.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 81px;\" /></p><p>At all odd integers from&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>21</mn></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;will have an extrema with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>17</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>21</mn></math>&nbsp;being points of minima &amp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>19</mn></math>&nbsp;being points of maxima.</p><p>So&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math>&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p>Hence&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>57</mn></math></p>",
